    <div class="wpd-space"></div>
    <div class="wpd-comment-link wpd-hidden">
    <span wpd-tooltip='Comment Link' wpd-tooltip-position='left'><i class='fas fa-link' aria-hidden='true' data-wpd-clipboard='https://familyspice.com/leftover-pulled-pork-ragu/#comment-94940'></i></span>
</div>
</div>
    
    <div class="wpd-comment-text">
    <p>I&#8217;m grateful for a recipe that doesn&#8217;t start with a whole pork butt, but(!) this was not nearly as saucy as the photo, and I had to double everything except the celery and wine to keep the ragu from being too dry. I also added some oregano as this is what brings out the flavor in tomatoes for me. It did turn out well and the leftovers should be even better. I normally cook polenta slowly in milk with butter and add salt and parmesan at the end, but I actually had some already prepared to use up, so this<span id='wpdiscuz-readmore-94940_0'><span class='wpdiscuz-hellip'>&hellip;&nbsp;</span><span class='wpdiscuz-readmore' title='Read more &raquo;'>Read more &raquo;</span></span></p>
</div>
    <div class="wpd-comment-footer">
